%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Butterfly
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 13
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Scale Dust
    AbilityDescription: 'PASSIVE. The wings shed dust onto whatever passes through
      them: an opposing pilot takes an all-element decaying debuff
      (VesselElementalDebuffBySkimmerEffect, classed VesselContact so an arena ward
      cannot cancel it) and a living creature''s heart WITHERS
      (SkimmerWitherLifeformByCrystalEffect, no speed gate - this is the slowest hull
      in the fleet and an overtake requirement would mean it could never kill
      anything that was not rooted). Charge is the BITE: the drain magnitude, priced
      off Broadside''s Strike class. The dust touches only the LIVING - it never
      removes mass; that is Space''s half.'
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Monarch
    UpgradeDescription: The dust bites twice as deep.
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Spread Wings
    AbilityDescription: 'HOLD. The wings open and the wake widens from a line of keys
      into a broad ribbon (SpreadWingsActionSO drives
      VesselPrismController.SetNormalizedXScale, which lerps over ~1.5s so a stroke
      reads as a stroke). It COSTS: holding drains the wing-energy meter, which
      refills only while the wings are shut, so what the pilot composes is WHERE the
      broad strokes go. Mass''s continuous dial is a different quantity - the trail
      prism''s VOLUME, authored as the trailVolume ElementalFloat on this vessel''s
      VesselPrismController (1 -> 2.5 at level 10, cube root per axis). Two
      quantities, not two dials on one number.'
    Input: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Mural
    UpgradeDescription: Spreading the wings is free - they stay open as long as you
      hold them.
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Wingreach
    AbilityDescription: 'PASSIVE. Opposing-domain mass that passes through the wings
      DISSOLVES - the Butterfly reduces enemy volume by soaring over it rather than
      by shooting it (SkimmerDamagePrismEffect with opposingDomainOnly set, so the
      wings never eat their own team''s wake). Space is the REACH: the skimmer''s
      Scale ElementalFloat, authored on the prefab, evaluated live - so a Butterfly
      that has fed on Space erases a wider swath of territory on every pass. It is
      the one ability whose whole expression is the vessel''s size.'
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Broadwing
    UpgradeDescription: The far-field wings join in - the dissolving swath widens to
      the outer wing radius.
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Fold
    AbilityDescription: 'HOLD. The vessel stops and a ghost of it appears; the two
      sticks place that ghost anywhere in the cell and letting go puts you there.
      XDiff is the RADIUS (thumbs in = the core, at rest = half way, thumbs out = the
      membrane - the dual-stick mix already reads 0/0.5/1 for exactly those, so
      nothing is rescaled), XSum and YSum are its azimuth and elevation, and YDiff
      goes on rolling the vessel as it always does - which rolls the camera, which
      carries the whole spherical frame with it. Outside a membrane the hold becomes
      a REACH along the heading instead. Time''s dial is the RECHARGE, the one dial
      that means something in both branches.'
    Input: 2
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Far Fold
    UpgradeDescription: The open-space fold reaches twice as far. Inside a membrane
      it changes nothing - the cell is already the limit.
